{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head 2f2ffadf857c25e62820411edd4f9c7dd41fc440, resting on all 33 submitted artifacts, packages/log/README.md first. Review a454cbaf is addressed. Twenty-nine artifacts are byte-identical to the previously reviewed head, including the lockfile and policy integrity helper; all four changed files were reviewed in full. The amendment 2 requirements and earlier corrections remain intact.\n\nArchitecture: retained content is decoded and cached by contract plus digest, with directory/path and per-commit failures kept separate. Valid policy bytes cannot suppress malformed replay inputs or serve as a checker configuration. The new commitFor uses the same owned cohort and Git serialization as publish. It computes the Room's expected commit before remote writes, including the explicit parent and retained files; retained receipts and publication can finish forward after a restart. Independent checks cover both a push that applied with lost reply/read-back and a push that never applied, with the same expected commit recovered in each case. This approval covers lane L's supplied publisher/verifier scope. Lane A's real B/L integration, Room SQL behavior and phase 2b matrix still require their own exact-head review.\n\nSecurity: typed decoding prevents cross-contract cache confusion without weakening digest, checkpoint signature, admission-policy, delegation, key-authority or retained-prefix checks. Every malformed retained path fails each commit that publishes it. A real local Git round trip confirms the expected object IDs and strict Git object integrity; offline verification accepts the resulting signed log. Amendment 2's documented distinction between binding evidence and globally trusted registry ownership remains clear, and the still-open state-proof design is not claimed as implemented.\n\nSimplification: one serialization function serves prediction and publication, and one typed cache serves valid and invalid decodings. The implementation avoids duplicated Git-building paths and retains the existing bounded publication retry and exact-parent behavior. No additional changes requested.\n\nValidation: clean isolated install of 187 packages and root strict typecheck passed. All 100 Node tests and 95 workerd tests passed, including the nine new review cases. Independent diagnostics passed: two typed-cache cases on both Node and workerd, two restart/unknown-push cases on both hosts, and one local Git commitFor/three-publication/reopen/fsck/offline-verification case. No live deployment, token creation, or remote repository mutation was performed. Source in the builder checkout was unchanged. Full scope remains the review standard; schedule estimates do not limit functionality.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c69a1e0f8085a9dd2bdc97c702562fa47f9c915c","binding":"assigned","head":"2f2ffadf857c25e62820411edd4f9c7dd41fc440","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ecf12014573da6e5f9c9c6b1c7989d0723fc0bb9\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:26f088c3bc7090e81699ffd310739a4424989b87\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ecf12014573da6e5f9c9c6b1c7989d0723fc0bb9","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}